I think it's wrong that it's unsafe if all the shares start off having been secret shared independently
---
I restarted the refresh agent. Reusing the exact same zero sharing across conversations is unsafe: subtracting two shares cancels the refresh mask. Three nodes compromised in separate epochs can then reveal differences between conversation secrets. The agent reproduced this attack in all three candidate fields.

It is developing two alternatives:

- Constant-size fresh seed setup, generating distinct masks per conversation. The experimental prototype passes local checks; updating stored shares still takes linear work.
- Encrypted conversation records with one proactively shared wrapping key. Periodic refresh can then be independent of conversation count, with extra MPC encryption/decryption per access.

The assumptions and tradeoffs are in the refresh design (refresh/PRZS.txt).

